{"id": "EUVD-2026-76486", "enisaUuid": "c15d488d-5cde-3cb5-b1c2-294fc56e91bc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm array: validate array block headers on read\n\narray_block_check() validates blocknr and csum and nothing else, while\nnode_check(), next to it, has bounded the structural fields since both\nwere written. dm_array_cursor_next() takes its loop bound from the\non-disk nr_entries and element_at() is unguarded pointer arithmetic, so\na count larger than the block holds keeps the cursor in one block while\nthe index grows past it and the read walks off the dm-bufio buffer --\ndm_cache_load_mappings() drives it once per cache block at activation.\n\nCheck the header against itself: reject a zero value_size, require\nmax_entries to equal calc_max_entries() for that value_size and block\nsize, and require nr_entries to fit. Equality rather than an upper bound,\nsince a count below the real capacity trips BUG_ON() in fill_ablock() and\ntrim_ablock(). Metadata dm-array writes satisfies all three.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:56", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e3b8f371c385c212b6e6f76c66f5b3f5bcfea62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/67adda7ed5da3e3b64f5b9021a02c21fb374fd9c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b33f76d33aaeacf3baf3370d8d64985169b36600", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9808ddffb4bc659352df3020cd84d9d864820ee5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2965787723084835b18dfe993cd450ebf5bd4540"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ccr8-4v7h-gw2w", "CVE-2026-89574"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1817dc68-e60a-3d4e-9687-e3f95fc4bc95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6513c29f44f2cc970c0e9fecfe5a6526c3e73025 <2965787723084835b18dfe993cd450ebf5bd4540"}, {"id": "2dfe5c94-85ed-3